<p>Amnesty International said a Nigerian military airstrike hit the crowded Tumfa market in the Zurmi district of Zamfara state on Sunday, killing at least 100 civilians. Daily Trust, cited by AllAfrica, reported at least 117 deaths and said residents described the casualties as including both bandits and civilians. Other Nigerian reports citing AFP put the toll at 72 or more and said some bodies were “blown beyond recognition”. A Nigerian military spokesman confirmed the strike in Zamfara state but said there was no verifiable evidence of civilian casualties; the military has denied accounts that civilians were harmed. Amnesty called for an investigation and said the strike was the latest deadly attack to kill civilians in northern Nigeria. Witnesses cited by Amnesty said military jets flew over the area around midday and returned about two hours later before striking the market. The group said the Tumfa attack was the second military airstrike in a month to kill scores of people at a crowded northern Nigerian market, after an April strike on a weekly market in Jilli killed around 200 civilians and prompted a military probe.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/PqtbWmRm0XGb9kYn6SjMeNz7Wxxvb_UtYmW7qPPjoGMkuUrPSzvfSVo9Fs7A6aq3X_OqV_mSTdO5-2v4L0EpqpT8sM_xs8nCkK7GZviV8DIC6ExDHGY7eUkw8piFCsiIbfdk1WnHHqFmN1W4aYFt-w3RQX2MgeRUcdYuFQuSf4JPIDB0zuWPwjsCNFXE8afo6iVxanGAtIR9PaO17IV8dgRHNM_ArMCNYR4o3GRazyzNnO5u7jMLwU6e_aMLBjultaKgQ3JA' alt='An airstrike hit Tumfa market in Zurmi district, claiming numerous lives in northern Nigeria.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Coordination concerns: Analysts blamed poor coordination between Nigeria’s air force and ground personnel for deadly mistakes in air operations.</li><li>Army stance: Army Chief of Staff Lt.-Gen. Waidi Shaibu reaffirmed the army’s commitment to defend Nigeria’s constitution while tackling insecurity.</li><li>Victim details: Residents said some of those killed at Tumfa were market vendors selling millet porridge and tofu.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Amnesty International: The rights group said the strikes were unlawful and showed disregard for civilian life. (<a href='https://english.aaj.tv/news/330458844/at-least-100-killed-in-nigerian-air-strike-on-zamfara-market-amnesty-says'>Aaj News</a>)</li><li>Nigerian military: In past comments on air operations, the military has said its strikes are intelligence-led and directed only at militant targets. (<a href='https://english.aaj.tv/news/330458844/at-least-100-killed-in-nigerian-air-strike-on-zamfara-market-amnesty-says'>Aaj News</a>)</li><li>Residents and community leaders: Garba Ibrahim Mashema, a community leader cited by AFP, said people in the area were at the mercy of bandits and had little choice but to go to the market. (<a href='https://thesun.ng/over-70-killed-as-military-bombs-zamfara-market/'>The Sun Nigeria</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-airstrike-kills-100-at-market-amnesty-says/a-77135993'>Nigeria airstrike kills 100 at market, Amnesty says</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/05/12/world/africa/nigeria-tumfa-market-strikes.html'>Nigerian Military Accused of War Crimes After Deadly Market Airstrikes</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/nigerian-airstrike-killed-100-civilians-market-amnesty-international-132882987'>Nigerian airstrike killed 100 civilians in a market, Amnesty International claims</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://allafrica.com/stories/202605130011.html'>Nigeria: Over 100 Killed in Zamfara Market Airstrike</a> - allafrica.com</li><li><a href='https://english.aaj.tv/news/330458844/at-least-100-killed-in-nigerian-air-strike-on-zamfara-market-amnesty-says'>At least 100 killed in Nigerian air strike on Zamfara market, Amnesty says</a> - aaj.tv</li><li><a href='https://eastleighvoice.co.ke/africa/349101/amnesty-accuses-nigerian-military-of-killing-over-100-civilians-in-zamfara